     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi D-RUGgies,<div><br></div><div>Hope you are all doing well. Please come by the Library in Room 360 tomorrow at 10am for our usual R work session. Since tomorrow is International Baby Day, I thought it might be fun to demo the <i style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">babynames</font></i><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"> package. Or just come and work on something you are interested in.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">More importantly, if you aren&#39;t sure where Shields Library Room 360* is, I&#39;ve made a treasure pirate map you can use to navigate with. As you can tell, it&#39;s extremely accurate and drawn to scale. R was not used in creating this map, but my 5-year old did provide some helpful suggestions. </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">The schedule for the remainder of the quarter looks like this...but we may shift things around as needed. If you&#39;d like to give a talk or have theme ideas, please let me know! If I can find a package or data that corresponds with the day, I plan on giving a little 5-10 min demo, just for fun. <br clear=\"all\"></span><div><br></div><div><b>SPRING 2017 D-RUG SCHEDULE (10am-12pm, Shields 360 in DSI)</b></div><div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><ul><li style=\"margin-left:15px\"><b>May 9: </b>Using RStudio/RMarkdown to create and maintain your CV (Ryan)</li><li style=\"margin-left:15px\"><b>May 16</b>: International Drawing Day: follow-up on GIS in R, intro to &quot;<font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b>sf</b></font>&quot; package for spatial data</li><li style=\"margin-left:15px\"><b>May 23: </b>Regular work session, <i>International Turtle Day</i></li><li style=\"margin-left:15px\"><b>May 30</b>: Working with rasters in R (Eric Holmes)</li><li style=\"margin-left:15px\"><b>June 6</b>: <span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Regular work session, </span><i>International Yo-Yo day</i></li></ul><div><i>Thanks,</i></div><div><i>Adios,<br>Ryan</i></div></div></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline\"><span> </span></span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></b></i></font></span><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><font size=\"1\"><i>&quot;When we try to pick out anything by itself, we find it hitched to everything else in the universe.&quot;<b><br>John Muir (My First Summer in the Sierra, 1911)</b></i></font></div><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b>----------------